    <mj-section background-color="#eff1f4" padding="1px 1px 1px 1px" border-radius="10px">
  <mj-column background-color="#fff" border-radius="10px" padding="0px">
    <mj-image
      border-radius="10px 10px 0 0"
      padding="0"
      width="600px"
      src="https://www.londonsummary.com/email/images/REPLACE_ME.jpg"
      alt="GSK site transformation"
      href="https://www.londonsummary.com/"
    />
    <mj-text
      padding="20px 20px 0px 20px"
      font-family="Austin News Text Web, TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif"
      color="#000000"
    >
      <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 400; margin: 0;">
        GSK site transformation
      </h2>
    </mj-text>
    <mj-text padding="0px 20px 0px 20px" font-family="Arial" color="#000000">
      <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; padding-top: 15px; margin: 0;">
  <strong>What happened?</strong> Hounslow councillors have approved plans to <a href="https://www.standard.co.uk/news/london/brentford-housing-development-glaxosmithkline-hounslow-b1274060.html" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #80011F; color: black;">redevelop the former GlaxoSmithKline headquarters</a> site in Brentford, West London, into a large mixed-use “15-minute neighbourhood. The regeneration project will deliver 1,522 homes, student accommodation for 506 people, and a 296-unit co-living building. Phase one includes five residential towers reaching up to 26 storeys and 761 homes, with a mix of private, social, and intermediate housing.
</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; padding-top: 15px; margin: 0;">
  <strong>Concerns: </strong>Opponents say the development’s height and scale could harm the area’s character and nearby heritage sites, such as Kew Gardens, Boston Manor, and Osterley House. Historic England warned that the tall towers may disrupt important sightlines and historic landscapes. There are also concerns about pressure on local infrastructure, including transport, schools, and healthcare services, as many residents will move in.
</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; padding-top: 15px; padding-bottom: 20px; margin: 0;">
  <strong>About the site:</strong> It served as GlaxoSmithKline's headquarters before operations moved elsewhere. Positioned close to key transport links, including the M4 corridor and nearby rail services, the location is considered strategically suitable for high-density regeneration. The surrounding area already includes offices, residential developments, and business parks, making it a prime candidate for mixed-use redevelopment.
</p>
    </mj-text>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
<mj-spacer height="20px" />
