  ">
    <a href="https://www.businesstimes.com.sg/international/bank-england-hit-5-inflation-risk-war-iran" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #80011F; color: black;">The Bank of England faces the possibility of inflation rising sharply again in the UK as global energy prices surge</a>. Economists warn inflation could climb close to 5%, more than double the bank’s 2% target, if oil and gas prices remain elevated. They estimated that inflation could reach 4.7% by September after Brent crude oil surged above $100 per barrel for the first time since 2022.
  </td>
</tr>
