    padding-bottom: 15px;
    padding-left: 0px;
  ">
    <a href="https://www.football.london/arsenal-fc/news/rodri-ban-man-city-arsenal-33558266" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #80011F; color: black;">Rodri has been fined £80,000 by The Football Association for comments he made about match officials after Manchester City drew 2-2 with Tottenham Hotspur</a>. Rodri publicly suggested referee Robert Jones was not “neutral,” questioning the integrity of the officiating after a controversial goal was allowed to stand. The FA charged him with improper conduct under Rule E3.1, which prohibits comments implying bias by officials.
  </td>
</tr>
<tr>
